            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Benjamin Fair",
                        "email": "benjaminfair@google.com",
                        "username": "BenjaminFair"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't seem Nuvoton-specific. Wouldn't the entity-map issue affect all BMCs?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree, maybe this should be the default everywhere.  I see a number of machines that already overwrite to an empty.\n\nIs the one at `./meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/ipmi/phosphor-ipmi-config/entity-map.json` even useful for anyone?  I don't know enough to weigh in on what this is useful for.  If it was just an example, we shouldn't apply it by default to any machine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tim Lee",
                        "email": "timlee660101@gmail.com",
                        "username": "timlee66"
                    },
                    "message": "Indeed, it should be the default empty for all BMCs. And according to author original design, the content has no real meaning. Thus, I should empty original entity-map.json instead of machine layer, right?\n\n```\n meta-phosphor: ipmi-config: add default entity map\n\n    Add an empty entity map json file.  The file is expected to be an array,\n    if it is present at all.  The file provided by default has no real\n    meaning to your system, therefore you are expected if you use the entity\n    records, to provide one for your system.\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure... but why isn't it empty now?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tim Lee",
                        "email": "timlee660101@gmail.com",
                        "username": "timlee66"
                    },
                    "message": "Due to I need to run ipmitool sdr to make sure no errors happen after change. Done."
                }
            ],
